01:29:43.450 --> 01:29:46.410
Wellby: Made it to the jungles north and east of Chardin.

01:29:49.870 --> 01:29:50.670
Wellby: To the eastern edge of the Green Sea.

01:29:50.730 --> 01:29:51.370
DM: Way northwards?

01:29:51.430 --> 01:29:52.590
Wellby: Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:29:52.650 --> 01:29:55.410
DM: Eastern edge of the Green Sea is not even on any of my maps.

01:29:56.270 --> 01:29:57.370
Wellby: Yeah, it's a long, long way.

01:29:57.450 --> 01:29:57.990
DM: What's out there?

01:29:59.669 --> 01:29:59.950
Wellby: Uh,

01:30:01.229 --> 01:30:02.930
Wellby: seagull kenku,

01:30:04.610 --> 01:30:09.110
Wellby: and moving islands, and pirates, and more pirates.

01:30:09.590 --> 01:30:13.570
Seeker: Now, there's an intrinsic difficulty in making maps of moving islands, isn't there?

01:30:15.170 --> 01:30:16.810
Wellby: I think it's a fascinating challenge.

01:30:18.890 --> 01:30:23.370
