Unknown: it, I thought maybe it would be an easy way to get everybody together if we put it out that we are...

02:19:20.746 --> 02:19:23.726
Delwath: The alf is telling the tale of

02:19:25.966 --> 02:19:26.826
Delwath: the Great War.

02:19:28.466 --> 02:19:29.546
Delwath: See who shows up.

02:19:29.546 --> 02:19:30.886
Seeker: And hosting a small feast.

02:19:30.886 --> 02:19:32.106
Delwath: And hosting a small feast.

02:19:33.566 --> 02:19:34.906
Delwath: University students

02:19:36.086 --> 02:19:37.246
Delwath: admitted by preference.

02:19:41.586 --> 02:19:44.546
Delwath: Those with tales of faraway places admitted by preference.

02:19:45.426 --> 02:19:47.706
Unknown: Well, why don't we just go try to talk to one person first?

02:19:47.706 --> 02:19:52.086
Delwath: 'Cause that could take a few days to spread news.

02:19:52.086 --> 02:19:54.306
Unknown: I think it's, I think it's not mutually exclusive.

02:19:54.646 --> 02:19:58.406
Wellby: Sure.

02:19:58.406 --> 02:20:02.406
Wellby: We'll start with the contacts we have and figure out how long we can be in town,

02:20:03.446 --> 02:20:04.766
Wellby: and if we get enough from them.

02:20:05.546 --> 02:20:07.746
Unknown: If we know we'll be in town longer, party,

02:20:09.146 --> 02:20:10.426
Wellby: more connections.

02:20:10.426 --> 02:20:10.626
Delwath: Yeah.

02:20:19.426 --> 02:20:19.606
Delwath: Mm-hmm.

02:20:19.606 --> 02:20:21.806
DM: This is the halfling band that's playing in the tavern.

02:20:22.206 --> 02:20:22.626
Seeker: Nice.

02:20:27.786 --> 02:20:31.426
Kenzo: So, um, I'll get a letter of introduction to the student Escobar in a day.

02:20:34.942 --> 02:20:38.422
Seeker: And didn't the, the map maker had, had another tubing connection?

02:20:40.582 --> 02:20:41.602
Wellby: Let's, uh, let's...

02:20:42.502 --> 02:20:43.782
Wellby: We've got Wendel here too.

02:20:44.742 --> 02:20:46.242
Wellby: This guy knows everybody and everything.

02:20:46.582 --> 02:20:47.222
DM: Let's talk to Wendel.

02:20:48.502 --> 02:20:49.202
Unknown: Yeah.

02:20:49.222 --> 02:20:57.382
DM: It's, yeah, so you, I mean, you've been sitting and talking for a while, like, the, the, like, busy rush has died down a little bit, and so you wave him over and he comes.

02:20:58.182 --> 02:21:00.122
DM: Um, he just does a little bit of a double take.

02:21:00.122 --> 02:21:04.822
DM: "Wellby, I saw you come in, but

02:21:06.602 --> 02:21:08.282
DM: traveling with some strange people now."

02:21:09.282 --> 02:21:13.142
Wellby: Yeah, they're not that strange once you get to know them, uh.

02:21:13.142 --> 02:21:14.862
DM: "I, I can believe that."

02:21:14.862 --> 02:21:16.342
Seeker: And then eventually, less strange.

02:21:16.342 --> 02:21:18.282
DM: "I, I've met a few elves.

02:21:19.062 --> 02:21:21.042
DM: Are you... You're not from Orenlas, are you?"

02:21:21.902 --> 02:21:22.282
Seeker: No.

02:21:22.282 --> 02:21:26.302
Wellby: [laughs]

02:21:26.362 --> 02:21:27.342
Delwath: Yeah, I've never been there.

02:21:27.342 --> 02:21:29.902
DM: "Huh.

02:21:29.902 --> 02:21:32.422
DM: Melindir, he's, um, doesn't

02:21:33.702 --> 02:21:35.842
DM: come this way much, but

02:21:37.782 --> 02:21:42.062
DM: yeah, he's around town a bit from, from Orenlas.

02:21:43.502 --> 02:21:43.702
DM: And then-"

02:21:43.702 --> 02:21:44.842
DM: I would like to talk to him.

02:21:44.842 --> 02:21:45.522
DM: "Dwarf?" [laughs]

02:21:45.522 --> 02:21:47.302
Unknown: Do we know this place name, Orenlas?

02:21:48.302 --> 02:21:49.742
Wellby: That's the elven kingdom.

02:21:49.842 --> 02:21:51.342
DM: It's like, you would've heard it.

02:21:51.342 --> 02:21:54.782
DM: It's like, there's an elven kingdom that's, like, south of,

02:21:56.382 --> 02:21:59.922
DM: of Sembara. There's like, near Tyrwingha, that's

02:22:02.142 --> 02:22:02.802
DM: what it is.

02:22:03.342 --> 02:22:03.782
Seeker: Okay.

02:22:03.782 --> 02:22:06.442
DM: "You, um,

02:22:07.662 --> 02:22:08.962
DM: what are you doing now, Wellby?"

02:22:10.082 --> 02:22:13.222
Wellby: We have been on the most amazing adventure over the last year.

02:22:13.222 --> 02:22:18.442
Wellby: We freed Nyan Surma, the trapped, uh, uh, ruler of Dunmar and-

02:22:18.842 --> 02:22:20.422
DM: Dunmar? That's pretty far away

02:22:20.422 --> 02:22:22.842
Wellby: ... started a civil war there a little bit by accident.

02:22:23.542 --> 02:22:26.362
Unknown: And then we went to Chardin and-

02:22:26.742 --> 02:22:28.022
DM: Even further away

02:22:28.022 --> 02:22:29.842
Unknown: ... not as nice as you would think it is.

02:22:30.122 --> 02:22:32.242
Unknown: Oh, nowhere is as nice as Tollen.

02:22:32.242 --> 02:22:34.702
Wellby: I am increasingly coming to understand this is true.

02:22:35.602 --> 02:22:38.682
Unknown: Uh, and then been a little bit here, there, and everywhere.

02:22:39.242 --> 02:22:40.602
Wellby: It's nice to be back here again.

02:22:40.602 --> 02:22:42.402
Unknown: "You in town long?"

02:22:42.402 --> 02:22:44.522
DM: [clears throat]

02:22:44.602 --> 02:22:46.222
Unknown: Uh, it depends. Probably not too long.

02:22:46.222 --> 02:22:48.982
Unknown: "Need a place to stay?

02:22:49.022 --> 02:22:54.502
DM: I've..." Looks at, "I've got rooms for you at least," looks at Wellby and Seeker.

02:22:55.462 --> 02:22:56.442
Wellby: Uh, probably.

02:22:56.442 --> 02:22:59.602
DM: "I have a few big folk rooms not taken."

02:23:00.682 --> 02:23:01.802
DM: Big folk. Nice.

02:23:02.482 --> 02:23:04.502
Wellby: What do you think? This does seem a lot nicer than

02:23:08.202 --> 02:23:10.402
Wellby: a big hulking flying boat.

02:23:11.262 --> 02:23:12.042
Delwath: But I think-

02:23:12.042 --> 02:23:16.342
DM: "Hey, Garrett, do we still have some big folk rooms?"

02:23:16.342 --> 02:23:24.342
DM: [laughs] This is like a guy, like a clearly overworked, much younger guy behind the bar, like gives him,

02:23:25.202 --> 02:23:28.902
DM: holds up his... "We still got four big folk rooms if you want a couple."

02:23:31.402 --> 02:23:32.782
Wellby: We'll just have dinner and think about it.

02:23:33.242 --> 02:23:35.502
Unknown: I was thinking of staying on the ship.

02:23:35.502 --> 02:23:38.062
Unknown: That's probably wise because people will find us-

02:23:38.062 --> 02:23:38.982
Delwath: On the ship

02:23:38.982 --> 02:23:39.182
Wellby: ... on the ship.

02:23:39.182 --> 02:23:39.542
Delwath: I'll stay on the ship.

02:23:39.542 --> 02:23:42.262
DM: "You're the flying ship elf."

02:23:44.042 --> 02:23:45.522
Delwath: Yes, Delwath at your service.

02:23:45.522 --> 02:23:47.442
DM: "Wendel.

02:23:49.342 --> 02:23:50.342
DM: Fascinating.

02:23:51.822 --> 02:23:53.582
Unknown: You know, there used to be flying ships.

02:23:56.042 --> 02:23:58.162
DM: My great-grandfather,

02:23:59.442 --> 02:24:03.022
DM: he said his grandfather told him a story that there used to be

02:24:04.362 --> 02:24:10.662
DM: an order of knights that protected Sembara from flying ships, and they fought a giant dragon

02:24:11.762 --> 02:24:15.522
DM: and crashed in the mountains, and that's what messed things up.

02:24:17.282 --> 02:24:18.622
DM: You think this is true?

02:24:18.622 --> 02:24:19.762
DM: He said it was a myth."

02:24:20.262 --> 02:24:21.542
Wellby: Oh, I think it's absolutely true.

02:24:23.482 --> 02:24:28.102
Unknown: Uh, [clears throat] in order of...

02:24:28.102 --> 02:24:29.222
Delwath: Messed what things up?

02:24:31.322 --> 02:24:34.582
DM: "Uh, it's never entirely clear, to be honest."

02:24:35.542 --> 02:24:36.882
Wellby: Something messed things up.

02:24:38.682 --> 02:24:40.622
Unknown: Your grandfather's grandfather, was it?

02:24:40.622 --> 02:24:42.742
DM: "Yeah."

02:24:44.302 --> 02:24:46.002
Unknown: So how long ago was the Great War?

02:24:47.282 --> 02:24:47.962
DM: 200 years.

02:24:49.222 --> 02:24:49.922
Seeker: So that would've been, like,

02:24:51.181 --> 02:24:51.862
Delwath: 200 years ago?

02:24:53.061 --> 02:24:53.342
DM: Yeah.

02:24:55.642 --> 02:24:58.562
Unknown: There were no flying ships in Sembara then.

02:24:58.562 --> 02:25:01.522
DM: "You sure?

02:25:02.722 --> 02:25:05.982
DM: 'Cause actually there were in our high school campaign."

02:25:05.982 --> 02:25:07.122
Delwath: There were flying ships?

02:25:07.122 --> 02:25:08.302
DM: You guys flew on a f-

02:25:09.582 --> 02:25:11.862
DM: Aaron, like, jumped off of a flying castle.

02:25:12.002 --> 02:25:12.482
Delwath: Oh.

02:25:12.482 --> 02:25:18.802
DM: You flew a flying castle to the valley where Rye got all these weird magic [paper rustling].

02:25:18.802 --> 02:25:18.902
Wellby: That's right.

02:25:18.922 --> 02:25:19.102
DM: Uh-

02:25:19.242 --> 02:25:20.442
Wellby: Which castle are you referring to?

02:25:20.522 --> 02:25:21.802
Delwath: Okay, I'll say I...

02:25:21.802 --> 02:25:23.342
Delwath: There was only one flying ship back then.

02:25:23.362 --> 02:25:25.762
Seeker: It was, it was less ship and more castle, but it was flying.

02:25:25.782 --> 02:25:27.182
DM: It was really a flying castle.

02:25:27.242 --> 02:25:31.822
Seeker: Yeah. Um, I, I did a ninth grade English assignment about it.

02:25:32.982 --> 02:25:38.242
Wellby: What? [laughs]

02:25:38.262 --> 02:25:39.802
Delwath: There, there are stories of, um,

02:25:41.762 --> 02:25:43.722
Delwath: I think Rye had a flying castle.

02:25:47.062 --> 02:25:51.082
Unknown: Sembara was, uh, not protecting themselves from them then.

02:25:53.262 --> 02:25:54.162
Kenzo: They were fighting together.

02:25:55.122 --> 02:25:59.542
DM: Oh, no, they, the flying, the knights protected Sembara from the flying castle.

02:25:59.542 --> 02:25:59.882
Unknown: [clears throat]

02:25:59.882 --> 02:26:00.782
DM: That's the story.

02:26:00.822 --> 02:26:00.982
Unknown: Hm.

02:26:01.762 --> 02:26:02.682
Kenzo: No.

02:26:02.682 --> 02:26:03.442
DM: You don't think so?

02:26:05.182 --> 02:26:05.442
Wellby: I was there.

02:26:05.442 --> 02:26:06.742
DM: Well, you're probably pretty old.

02:26:08.522 --> 02:26:09.262
DM: Looks up at you.

02:26:09.602 --> 02:26:10.302
Seeker: Yeah, I was there.

02:26:12.062 --> 02:26:12.582
DM: Fair enough.

02:26:13.202 --> 02:26:14.362
Wellby: Wait, we were the knights?

02:26:15.262 --> 02:26:15.822
Wellby: That's funny.

02:26:16.982 --> 02:26:18.382
Delwath: No, we were the flying castle.

02:26:18.902 --> 02:26:19.522
Wellby: Right.

02:26:19.542 --> 02:26:21.162
Unknown: The knights were fighting us off.

02:26:21.182 --> 02:26:21.302
DM: Yes.

02:26:21.302 --> 02:26:21.882
Delwath: Not really.

02:26:23.142 --> 02:26:24.742
Wellby: Wait, maybe-

02:26:24.802 --> 02:26:32.482
Delwath: The rumor is we were the bad guys, and Sembara was protecting Sem- the, the Sembaran knights were protecting Sembara from us.

02:26:33.702 --> 02:26:35.242
Seeker: Ah, from a castle like

02:26:36.474 --> 02:26:37.574
Seeker: The way Tim was saying it-

02:26:37.634 --> 02:26:40.774
DM: No, no. It was the flying castle flew around protecting Sembara.

02:26:41.454 --> 02:26:42.014
DM: Oh.

02:26:42.014 --> 02:26:42.134
DM: Yeah.

02:26:42.134 --> 02:26:43.354
Seeker: Yeah, we were the protectors. I was wondering about that.

02:26:43.394 --> 02:26:48.574
Delwath: No, no, no. Sorry. I thought you said the knights protected Sembara from a flying castle that was attacking.

02:26:48.634 --> 02:26:50.474
DM: Yeah, yeah. They were on the flying castle.

02:26:50.554 --> 02:26:52.214
Delwath: Oh, no, I wouldn't have said that then.

02:26:52.434 --> 02:26:53.594
DM: Sorry. I thought you meant-

02:26:54.154 --> 02:26:54.194
Unknown: Yeah

02:26:54.194 --> 02:26:55.794
Delwath: ... the knight's job was to stop-

02:26:55.794 --> 02:26:56.694
Delwath: Was to protect, right

02:26:56.694 --> 02:26:57.794
DM: ... the flying castle-

02:26:58.354 --> 02:26:58.534
Unknown: Yeah

02:26:58.534 --> 02:26:59.854
DM: ... from getting into Sembara.

02:26:59.854 --> 02:27:01.814
Seeker: But no, he was saying the knights were on the flying castle.

02:27:01.854 --> 02:27:01.874
DM: Yeah.

02:27:02.494 --> 02:27:03.374
Seeker: And the knights were dead.

02:27:03.474 --> 02:27:04.774
DM: Yeah, well, fine, then I would've said

02:27:06.214 --> 02:27:06.854
DM: something different.

02:27:06.854 --> 02:27:07.194
Delwath: Flying airship.

02:27:07.694 --> 02:27:07.854
DM: Yeah.

02:27:13.434 --> 02:27:13.654
Unknown: Very well. Okay.

02:27:13.654 --> 02:27:16.054
Wellby: What's the, what's the story with the, um...

02:27:16.074 --> 02:27:17.094
Wellby: What's the name of the fae?

02:27:17.754 --> 02:27:19.774
Delwath: Oh, um, Caelynn.

02:27:19.774 --> 02:27:20.534
DM: Caelynn.

02:27:21.474 --> 02:27:24.774
Wellby: Caelynn. What's the story with Caelynn?

02:27:24.774 --> 02:27:26.534
Wellby: I don't remember hearing much about her as a kid.

02:27:26.534 --> 02:27:31.274
DM: [sighs] I think she's a fraud.

02:27:31.754 --> 02:27:31.914
Wellby: Hm.

02:27:34.254 --> 02:27:35.034
DM: Oh.

02:27:35.034 --> 02:27:35.894
Wellby: What, is she fae?

02:27:37.394 --> 02:27:38.654
DM: Oh, she's definitely fae.

02:27:40.494 --> 02:27:40.933
DM: But like,

02:27:42.674 --> 02:27:44.354
Unknown: thousand years old, I don't buy that.

02:27:44.874 --> 02:27:46.074
DM: We'd have more stories.

02:27:49.114 --> 02:27:49.254
Wellby: Hm.

02:27:52.054 --> 02:27:53.014
DM: Eh. I think she, uh...

02:27:57.094 --> 02:28:02.254
DM: I don't know.

02:28:02.254 --> 02:28:04.154
DM: There's so many conflicting rumors.

02:28:04.154 --> 02:28:05.974
DM: I feel like she must spread them herself.

02:28:06.974 --> 02:28:07.034
Wellby: Hm.

02:28:07.054 --> 02:28:07.894
DM: Like, for example.

02:28:08.234 --> 02:28:08.534
Wellby: Hm.

02:28:09.174 --> 02:28:10.754
DM: Her prophecies always come true.

02:28:10.794 --> 02:28:11.194
Wellby: Hm.

02:28:11.194 --> 02:28:11.474
Kenzo: What's that?

02:28:11.474 --> 02:28:12.994
DM: Or her prophecies never come true.

02:28:13.654 --> 02:28:13.814
Wellby: Hm.

02:28:16.394 --> 02:28:18.654
DM: Both of those. People say both of those things.

02:28:18.654 --> 02:28:19.454
Seeker: Can't be both.

02:28:22.254 --> 02:28:23.054
Seeker: Can't both be true.

02:28:25.214 --> 02:28:27.474
DM: I suspect her prophecies sometimes come true.

02:28:29.014 --> 02:28:29.614
DM: Like most folk.

02:28:29.634 --> 02:28:30.254
Wellby: Practical, practical

02:28:32.114 --> 02:28:32.254
Wellby: man.

02:28:32.254 --> 02:28:34.394
DM: So she spreads rumors to ease people.

02:28:40.154 --> 02:28:40.394
DM: But

02:28:41.474 --> 02:28:42.954
DM: definitely some magic about her,

02:28:43.874 --> 02:28:45.134
DM: that's unquestionable.

02:28:45.994 --> 02:28:48.314
Unknown: She's not human. She's clearly fae.

02:28:48.314 --> 02:28:51.554
DM: I've never met her, but stories people tell, she has

02:28:54.694 --> 02:28:55.814
DM: alien eyes.

02:28:56.594 --> 02:28:57.474
DM: Bright green.

02:28:58.374 --> 02:28:58.554
Wellby: Hm.

02:28:58.554 --> 02:29:00.174
Unknown: Nothing you've ever seen.

02:29:00.174 --> 02:29:00.814
Wellby: Dangerous?

02:29:02.294 --> 02:29:04.554
Unknown: All fae are dangerous. You should know this, Wellby.

02:29:04.594 --> 02:29:06.794
Unknown: Yeah, it's true. Been in some troubles.

02:29:07.734 --> 02:29:10.174
DM: Dangerous, not the same as evil.

02:29:17.174 --> 02:29:17.254
Unknown: Yeah.

02:29:17.254 --> 02:29:18.634
DM: But she clearly knows a lot.

02:29:22.574 --> 02:29:23.254
Wellby: How do you find her?

02:29:24.834 --> 02:29:28.314
Unknown: If we were to go looking.

02:29:28.314 --> 02:29:28.754
DM: She has a

02:29:30.234 --> 02:29:30.734
DM: house,

02:29:31.774 --> 02:29:33.334
DM: I guess, up by the university.

02:29:33.354 --> 02:29:35.314
DM: I don't know if she actually sleeps there or not.

02:29:35.314 --> 02:29:36.434
DM: An office maybe.

02:29:37.574 --> 02:29:38.554
Kenzo: All right.

02:29:38.554 --> 02:29:39.714
DM: Like, she, uh...

02:29:44.234 --> 02:29:46.974
DM: People come to her when they need things or want things.

02:29:48.734 --> 02:29:49.194
DM: She must

02:29:50.214 --> 02:29:51.474
DM: have a reason to stay.

02:29:58.754 --> 02:29:59.794
DM: I think you just ask.

02:30:00.354 --> 02:30:03.674
DM: All right.

02:30:03.674 --> 02:30:04.334
DM: My, uh...

02:30:06.014 --> 02:30:06.194
DM: Hm.

02:30:07.674 --> 02:30:08.814
DM: I bet you, um...

02:30:12.274 --> 02:30:13.654
DM: Uh, Nika could tell you.

02:30:16.474 --> 02:30:17.174
DM: She's, uh,

02:30:18.634 --> 02:30:20.534
DM: associated with the university.

02:30:21.394 --> 02:30:23.734
DM: Not really a student anymore, I guess.

02:30:25.154 --> 02:30:26.854
DM: Hangs around here sometimes.

02:30:27.674 --> 02:30:29.294
Unknown: Mostly gets sailor types, but

02:30:30.634 --> 02:30:35.974
DM: I guess there's a lot of people around the university who will pay for a good story.

02:30:37.494 --> 02:30:37.834
DM: So

02:30:39.554 --> 02:30:41.574
DM: she comes and listens. Smart, I guess.

02:30:44.874 --> 02:30:48.054
DM: I mean, it's not like we're keeping the stories to ourselves.

02:30:49.794 --> 02:30:50.514
Kenzo: Never have.

02:30:52.673 --> 02:30:54.754
DM: I guess you could ask her. She comes around

02:30:56.334 --> 02:30:57.293
DM: most nights.

02:30:58.674 --> 02:31:04.194
DM: I don't know if she'll be in tonight or not, but usually comes in around 8:00 or 9:00 when the day is wrapping up.

02:31:06.394 --> 02:31:08.314
Wellby: What is the news from Dunmar around here?

02:31:10.094 --> 02:31:10.654
DM: Dunmar?

02:31:13.014 --> 02:31:13.214
Unknown: Yeah.

02:31:16.514 --> 02:31:19.214
DM: Eh. Can't say I've had much news from Dunmar recently.

02:31:26.774 --> 02:31:27.274
DM: Uh, not many

02:31:28.574 --> 02:31:29.494
DM: of our folk have

02:31:31.014 --> 02:31:33.074
DM: come this way from there this season.

02:31:33.694 --> 02:31:33.994
DM: It's taking them a while.

02:31:33.994 --> 02:31:37.634
Kenzo: Must take, like, news from Dunmar would take, like, months and months to get here.

02:31:37.674 --> 02:31:39.354
Unknown: So long, right? To come overland.

02:31:39.674 --> 02:31:41.374
Seeker: Yeah. Just take forever to get here.

02:31:42.614 --> 02:31:43.534
DM: There's rumors

02:31:46.054 --> 02:31:46.614
DM: of war and

02:31:47.654 --> 02:31:49.634
DM: trouble, especially in the passes.

02:32:01.054 --> 02:32:01.154
Wellby: Hm.

02:32:01.154 --> 02:32:02.014
DM: But yeah, not...

02:32:03.554 --> 02:32:05.614
DM: Strangely little news, I would say.

02:32:10.034 --> 02:32:13.374
Wellby: I'll give you the quick rundown on the political situation in Dunmar.

