02:47:02.382 --> 02:47:03.062
Wellby: What do you charge?

02:47:07.722 --> 02:47:08.962
DM: She looks around at you.

02:47:09.722 --> 02:47:12.482
DM: For you, hmm, 10 gold a day.

02:47:14.502 --> 02:47:18.922
Unknown: Delwath would kind of roll his eyes.

02:47:18.922 --> 02:47:24.902
DM: She takes one glance at Delwath, is like, "Don't pretend that that's a big expense for you."

02:47:25.342 --> 02:47:26.042
Kenzo: Is it my soul Scepter?

02:47:28.022 --> 02:47:28.222
Wellby: Hmm.

02:47:28.242 --> 02:47:29.962
Unknown: Just don't like being taken advantage of.

02:47:30.382 --> 02:47:32.722
Kenzo: Telepathically to everybody, I don't like this person.

02:47:32.722 --> 02:47:35.222
DM: I don't think you have telepathy after this time.

02:47:35.882 --> 02:47:36.922
Seeker: Yeah, you're probably right.

02:47:36.942 --> 02:47:38.382
DM: It's been way more than an hour.

02:47:38.382 --> 02:47:41.262
DM: I don't think Seekers like spending 10 minutes doing a ritual.

02:47:41.262 --> 02:47:46.342
Unknown: I think Wellby has, has learned like the, the look though from Kenzo.

02:47:46.702 --> 02:47:46.822
Unknown: Right.

02:47:46.822 --> 02:47:48.602
Unknown: Like Kenzo has a particular look that's like-

02:47:48.622 --> 02:47:49.322
DM: That's like...

02:47:49.562 --> 02:47:50.962
Kenzo: My look is like, "Who the fuck is this bitch?"

02:47:51.782 --> 02:47:53.562
Unknown: Um, Delwath will say to her, "Uh,

02:47:55.522 --> 02:47:56.802
Delwath: 10 gold is, um,

02:47:58.522 --> 02:48:01.142
Delwath: an awful lot to be shown around for a day.

02:48:02.822 --> 02:48:06.722
Delwath: And you can, uh, probably make quite a bit just from stories of us."

02:48:08.042 --> 02:48:09.002
DM: You got a good story?

02:48:10.102 --> 02:48:10.542
Kenzo: Many.

02:48:11.542 --> 02:48:12.842
Delwath: Didn't you hear of Wellby's earlier?

02:48:14.082 --> 02:48:15.202
DM: Yeah, I already got that one.

02:48:16.522 --> 02:48:17.602
Wellby: How did you get that one?

02:48:19.762 --> 02:48:21.142
DM: What do you mean how? I listened.

02:48:22.442 --> 02:48:23.362
Wellby: Yeah. What-

02:48:26.182 --> 02:48:29.202
DM: Some nice little tidbit of news that some people will like

02:48:32.462 --> 02:48:35.282
Delwath: I mean, I'm not wrong, right? 10 gold a day is a ridiculously large...

02:48:35.282 --> 02:48:37.982
Unknown: That's like what she should earn in a month or more.

02:48:38.462 --> 02:48:46.122
DM: Mm, no, like a gold, a gold is a, is a, like a decent skilled laborer would earn a gold per day.

02:48:48.882 --> 02:48:49.622
DM: So it's like,

02:48:51.142 --> 02:48:51.562
DM: you know.

02:48:51.642 --> 02:48:51.882
Wellby: Yeah.

02:48:51.882 --> 02:48:59.342
Delwath: So it's not like I was thinking, I was thinking it, silver would be like a daily wage, so that's why.

02:48:59.342 --> 02:49:03.562
Unknown: Silver would be daily wage for like a, you know, common laborer or something probably.

02:49:03.562 --> 02:49:05.142
Unknown: Look, I'm all in on this person.

02:49:05.762 --> 02:49:06.162
Seeker: Why?

02:49:07.162 --> 02:49:07.742
Seeker: Based on what?

02:49:09.482 --> 02:49:11.122
Unknown: What, what, what's a fae?

02:49:11.141 --> 02:49:15.502
Wellby: Because she was able to [dramatic sound] articulate-

02:49:15.562 --> 02:49:15.762
Unknown: Oops

02:49:15.762 --> 02:49:19.322
Wellby: ... what the actual transaction that the fae was offering was

02:49:20.902 --> 02:49:24.102
Wellby: in a way that none of the other people who talked about it could articulate.

02:49:24.342 --> 02:49:25.442
Kenzo: Wait, what did Chatuchu do that?

02:49:27.022 --> 02:49:32.482
Wellby: She said what's actually happening there is not about secret keeping or trading of information.

02:49:33.062 --> 02:49:37.842
Wellby: The service that the fae provides is allowing you to forget a thing that's happened.

02:49:38.802 --> 02:49:42.702
Unknown: But I bet you it's more complicated than that too, 'cause it's not always about...

02:49:43.662 --> 02:49:46.642
Delwath: I don't think, I think that is a service, not the service.

02:49:47.462 --> 02:49:50.902
Wellby: Still, it suggests an understanding of the dynamics of what's going on.

02:49:51.562 --> 02:49:55.542
Kenzo: Well, I think the bigger question is, does she actually have relationships with people that we wanna connect with?

02:49:56.222 --> 02:49:56.502
DM: Yeah.

02:49:56.502 --> 02:49:58.262
Kenzo: Is she gonna, is she gonna help facilitate?

02:49:58.262 --> 02:50:00.882
Kenzo: She has demonstrated nothing that says that she knows anybody about anything.

02:50:00.942 --> 02:50:02.182
DM: I mean, you're all sitting in a-

02:50:02.182 --> 02:50:02.902
Wellby: We're gonna reflect, sir.

02:50:03.102 --> 02:50:04.362
DM: Okay. We're gonna like...

02:50:04.442 --> 02:50:06.142
Unknown: Yeah, let's, let's... So,

02:50:07.402 --> 02:50:07.662
Kenzo: um,

02:50:12.702 --> 02:50:13.602
Delwath: 10 gold.

02:50:16.202 --> 02:50:18.282
DM: Come on, I know you came in in a flying ship.

02:50:18.622 --> 02:50:21.142
Wellby: I'll say telepathically to you, like, "Wha...

02:50:21.682 --> 02:50:25.422
Wellby: How many gold are you carrying on you at this moment?"

02:50:26.622 --> 02:50:27.082
Seeker: What's your name?

02:50:27.942 --> 02:50:28.462
DM: Nika.

02:50:28.702 --> 02:50:29.122
Delwath: 400.

02:50:29.662 --> 02:50:29.922
Wellby: Nika,

02:50:32.702 --> 02:50:35.862
Kenzo: can you connect us with somebody knowledgeable about volcanoes?

02:50:38.742 --> 02:50:45.302
Delwath: The way you're supposed to play this, Nika, is you ask for a small amount now, reasonable, right?

02:50:45.302 --> 02:50:46.722
Delwath: And then when you're helpful,

02:50:47.782 --> 02:50:48.482
Kenzo: you get more,

02:50:49.582 --> 02:51:00.530
Delwath: right? You don't play it by starting with the big ask, acting like we have no idea that that's a big ask, right

02:51:00.530 --> 02:51:01.990
DM: That's the way you play it

02:51:01.990 --> 02:51:03.550
DM: Are all elves like this?

02:51:03.550 --> 02:51:04.570
Seeker: Condescending? Yeah.

02:51:04.570 --> 02:51:07.170
Wellby: 100% of the elves I have traveled with are like this.

02:51:08.710 --> 02:51:09.170
DM: Basic question.

02:51:09.170 --> 02:51:09.990
DM: Do you wanna try again?

02:51:10.870 --> 02:51:14.890
Kenzo: Listen, Nika, can you connect us with the information we're interested in?

02:51:16.490 --> 02:51:17.750
DM: About volcanoes?

02:51:17.750 --> 02:51:19.130
DM: Why do you wanna know about volcanoes?

02:51:19.230 --> 02:51:20.270
Kenzo: Can you do it or not?

02:51:20.650 --> 02:51:22.930
DM: There's lots of people who know about volcanoes.

02:51:22.970 --> 02:51:23.030
DM: You can-

02:51:23.050 --> 02:51:25.690
Wellby: We want to know a volcano that's connected to the elemental plane of fire

02:51:29.730 --> 02:51:32.050
Unknown: There is somebody you could speak to.

02:51:32.050 --> 02:51:32.550
Kenzo: Who is that?

02:51:33.510 --> 02:51:34.790
DM: Not easy to, though.

02:51:38.390 --> 02:51:38.850
DM: Umli

02:51:39.970 --> 02:51:42.630
DM: the Exile. She's a Stoneborn,

02:51:43.670 --> 02:51:45.190
DM: smith, a metalworker.

02:51:47.550 --> 02:51:47.750
DM: Shapes

02:51:50.610 --> 02:51:53.010
DM: steel and iron with some

02:51:53.810 --> 02:51:56.310
Unknown: magical connection to fire.

02:51:56.910 --> 02:51:58.890
Unknown: Hmm. That was interesting.

02:51:58.890 --> 02:51:59.530
Kenzo: Do you know where she is?

02:52:03.170 --> 02:52:04.550
Kenzo: Now you're starting to sound valuable.

02:52:05.190 --> 02:52:06.030
DM: Okay, Alf.

02:52:07.210 --> 02:52:15.130
DM: Maybe if you give me five silver, I will give you this piece of information, and then we can negotiate a higher price for more information.

02:52:15.510 --> 02:52:17.330
DM: Is that how I'm supposed to do it?

02:52:18.330 --> 02:52:18.410
Unknown: That's great.

02:52:18.410 --> 02:52:19.990
Kenzo: It's a little less attitude, yeah.

02:52:19.990 --> 02:52:21.210
Unknown: [laughs]

02:52:21.210 --> 02:52:22.410
Seeker: I think, I think you deserve it.

02:52:22.430 --> 02:52:23.650
Kenzo: Five silver is fair.

02:52:23.650 --> 02:52:24.970
Delwath: Five silver is a fair price.

02:52:25.230 --> 02:52:26.090
Seeker: It's a very fair price.

02:52:28.550 --> 02:52:29.910
DM: Tricky thing about Umli,

02:52:31.310 --> 02:52:34.410
DM: she doesn't teach open lectures or...

02:52:38.210 --> 02:52:40.670
DM: She only takes private students who are

02:52:42.710 --> 02:52:44.110
DM: the most skilled and

02:52:45.450 --> 02:52:47.830
DM: dedicated to working with rare metals.

02:52:48.350 --> 02:52:49.450
Wellby: Perhaps I could apply.

02:52:51.870 --> 02:52:54.510
Kenzo: Or perhaps she'd be interested in coming to a Stoneborn ship.

02:52:56.110 --> 02:52:56.750
Delwath: A giant ship.

02:52:56.910 --> 02:52:57.030
Unknown: A giant ship.

02:52:57.030 --> 02:52:57.370
Wellby: Right.

02:52:57.750 --> 02:52:58.490
DM: A giant ship.

02:52:58.610 --> 02:52:58.850
Unknown: Um-

02:52:59.290 --> 02:53:01.270
DM: If you want to try and speak with her,

02:53:04.170 --> 02:53:05.210
DM: your best bet,

02:53:07.250 --> 02:53:07.610
DM: uh,

02:53:08.889 --> 02:53:12.630
DM: every week on Tuesdays, which happens to be tomorrow-

02:53:13.690 --> 02:53:14.010
Kenzo: Perfect

02:53:16.130 --> 02:53:20.370
DM: ... she takes interviews for new students at a place I can lead you to,

02:53:21.610 --> 02:53:23.210
DM: if you hire me as your guide.

02:53:27.570 --> 02:53:29.210
Unknown: Is she affiliated with the university?

02:53:30.510 --> 02:53:31.410
Kenzo: Is she affiliated with Tinn?

02:53:31.650 --> 02:53:32.610
Seeker: What does she look like?

02:53:32.610 --> 02:53:34.590
Kenzo: With Tinn. [laughs]

02:53:34.590 --> 02:53:36.390
Unknown: I'm gonna, I'm gonna ask a few leading questions-

02:53:36.410 --> 02:53:36.610
Unknown: She's attractive

02:53:36.610 --> 02:53:37.950
Kenzo: ... because I need a good description of her.

02:53:40.110 --> 02:53:41.450
DM: What does she look like?

02:53:41.450 --> 02:53:41.810
DM: Uh,

02:53:43.750 --> 02:53:44.710
DM: gray skin,

02:53:46.370 --> 02:53:47.110
DM: serious.

02:53:50.030 --> 02:53:50.710
Seeker: Like a Stoneborn.

02:53:51.610 --> 02:53:52.870
Kenzo: There's no way it's not a plan.

02:53:52.870 --> 02:53:53.970
DM: Purple eyes.

02:53:58.230 --> 02:53:59.210
DM: Like a Stoneborn.

02:53:59.210 --> 02:54:07.030
Unknown: [sighs]

02:54:07.030 --> 02:54:08.030
Delwath: Yes. We...

02:54:09.050 --> 02:54:11.850
Wellby: Well, we just, like, nodding and pantomime.

02:54:14.170 --> 02:54:15.090
Seeker: W- okay. We-

02:54:15.170 --> 02:54:18.390
DM: Shall I meet you here tomorrow morning then, or around lunchtime?

02:54:21.610 --> 02:54:30.890
Wellby: Yeah, but tell everyone that we drove a really hard bargain, and you barely got anything out of us, or everyone in this city is gonna charge us the same absurd rates that you are.

02:54:33.090 --> 02:54:34.150
DM: I'll keep your secret.

02:54:35.690 --> 02:54:36.970
Delwath: Wait, we're really giving her 10 gold?

02:54:42.530 --> 02:54:44.530
Unknown: Come by lunchtime tomorrow.

02:54:44.530 --> 02:54:45.870
DM: I'll meet you here and take you up there.

02:54:46.510 --> 02:54:46.990
Seeker: Great.

02:54:48.550 --> 02:54:49.930
Delwath: I mean, I'll say this out loud.

02:54:49.930 --> 02:54:53.050
Delwath: You know, I could just find the guy if we really wanted to.

02:54:53.050 --> 02:54:54.030
Kenzo: It's a girl.

02:54:54.030 --> 02:54:55.410
Seeker: Find the woman if we wanted to.

02:54:58.110 --> 02:55:00.010
Seeker: But yeah, sure, we'll pay.

02:55:00.750 --> 02:55:01.330
Seeker: Why not?

02:55:01.330 --> 02:55:02.850
Seeker: I think we want an introduction.

02:55:02.850 --> 02:55:03.390
Seeker: Can't hurt.

02:55:04.510 --> 02:55:10.950
Delwath: I mean, it can't be that hard to find a Stoneborn who you could look at and scry, right?

02:55:10.970 --> 02:55:12.250
Wellby: Oh, elves.

02:55:13.610 --> 02:55:14.030
Kenzo: Anyway.

02:55:16.050 --> 02:55:18.010
Unknown: You can scry somebody that just gives out a description?

02:55:18.010 --> 02:55:18.210
Unknown: Yeah.

02:55:19.189 --> 02:55:20.650
Delwath: They get a plus five to their save, but

02:55:22.129 --> 02:55:26.090
Delwath: you actually have it pretty good. Even with a plus five to their save, it's still a DC 13.

02:55:27.430 --> 02:55:29.790
Unknown: It's hard to avoid Delan scrying.

02:55:31.090 --> 02:55:32.210
Kenzo: You're so creepy.

02:55:32.850 --> 02:55:34.650
Delwath: It is a little creepy, I admit.

02:55:35.050 --> 02:55:35.330
Kenzo: Yeah.

02:55:35.330 --> 02:55:37.010
Unknown: Like, admittedly, a little creepy.

02:55:37.050 --> 02:55:38.030
Kenzo: Yeah.

02:55:38.030 --> 02:55:38.210
Unknown: So...

02:55:39.330 --> 02:55:39.790
DM: Ew.

02:55:40.370 --> 02:55:41.590
Seeker: How would Seeker say this?

02:55:43.810 --> 02:55:44.130
Seeker: Um,

02:55:45.650 --> 02:55:47.810
Seeker: it's worth keeping our wits about us

02:55:48.690 --> 02:55:51.570
Unknown: with this student, who has now left the table, presumably.

02:55:51.570 --> 02:55:51.870
DM: Yeah.

02:55:55.030 --> 02:55:57.750
Seeker: I can't tell you exactly why I feel this way, but

02:55:58.830 --> 02:56:00.770
Seeker: there's just something of the fae about her to me.

02:56:01.530 --> 02:56:03.930
Unknown: I soul sighted then, Tim. What, what did you, what did she say to you?

02:56:05.190 --> 02:56:05.550
DM: Um-

02:56:06.950 --> 02:56:08.270
Wellby: Oh, shit. Hmm

02:56:08.270 --> 02:56:08.270
DM: ...

02:56:10.310 --> 02:56:12.030
Unknown: I, I mean, she was kinda, um,

02:56:15.990 --> 02:56:16.950
DM: curious about you.

02:56:18.870 --> 02:56:23.130
DM: N- not like in any partic- not any particularly strong in any way.

02:56:23.130 --> 02:56:23.210
DM: Like-

02:56:23.270 --> 02:56:23.890
Kenzo: What level is she?

02:56:24.410 --> 02:56:26.250
Unknown: Like a normal... Not any level.

02:56:26.750 --> 02:56:27.490
Seeker: Not any level?

02:56:27.510 --> 02:56:27.730
DM: Yeah.

02:56:28.610 --> 02:56:30.230
Unknown: Strengths, uh, highest, lowest?

02:56:31.150 --> 02:56:35.110
DM: Um, like, intelligence and

02:56:36.850 --> 02:56:38.910
DM: dexterity probably highest.

02:56:39.470 --> 02:56:40.050
DM: Yeah.

02:56:40.050 --> 02:56:40.190
DM: Like-

02:56:40.190 --> 02:56:48.370
Wellby: As a sidebar, if she was a thousand-year-old fae, presumably she'd have a way of masking that, even against detection, in an unjust world.

02:56:48.370 --> 02:56:50.050
DM: Yeah. I would think so.

02:56:50.050 --> 02:56:50.390
Seeker: Yeah. Yes.

02:56:51.370 --> 02:56:53.670
Unknown: What makes you think that she's got fae-ish qualities?

02:56:53.970 --> 02:57:01.430
Seeker: Like I said, I, I can't put my finger on anything in particular, but having had the experience that we did, you know, Agata was-

02:57:02.270 --> 02:57:05.330
Seeker: Well, wrapped around my finger is not quite the right phrase either

02:57:05.330 --> 02:57:07.430
Kenzo: I, I, I trust, I trust totally what you're saying right now.

02:57:07.790 --> 02:57:08.890
Delwath: Uh, we should be very cautious.

02:57:08.930 --> 02:57:09.490
Wellby: Oh, I love it.

02:57:10.290 --> 02:57:10.550
Seeker: It just-

02:57:10.630 --> 02:57:11.350
Wellby: This is wonderful.

02:57:13.130 --> 02:57:14.070
Seeker: Like I said, it just could-

02:57:14.150 --> 02:57:14.490
Wellby: This is good

02:57:14.490 --> 02:57:15.570
Seeker: ... we need to keep our wits about us.

02:57:16.930 --> 02:57:18.950
Wellby: If she is, this is the best possible outcome.

02:57:19.750 --> 02:57:20.490
Delwath: Because...

02:57:21.590 --> 02:57:22.110
Wellby: Access

02:57:22.930 --> 02:57:25.130
Unknown: to anything and everything.

02:57:27.950 --> 02:57:31.450
Wellby: I mean, to people, to the city, to secrets, to information.

02:57:32.370 --> 02:57:36.890
Wellby: If she is 100 years or 1,000 years of secrets, like that's...

02:57:37.610 --> 02:57:38.190
Delwath: That's remarkable.

02:57:38.210 --> 02:57:48.870
Seeker: Also worth, worth noting that the motivations of Fae are sometimes inscrutable to us of this plane, and that she could have some trickery installed.

02:57:48.870 --> 02:57:51.650
Delwath: And also not every Fae is, um...

02:57:52.350 --> 02:57:52.850
Delwath: What's her name?

02:57:53.670 --> 02:57:54.090
Delwath: The gata?

02:57:55.170 --> 02:57:55.730
Wellby: No, the...

02:57:56.530 --> 02:57:57.070
Delwath: Caelynn?

02:57:57.070 --> 02:57:58.430
Delwath: Caelynn.

02:57:58.490 --> 02:57:58.710
Delwath: Right.

02:57:58.770 --> 02:58:01.270
Wellby: True. This is also true, and there's lots of Fae around here.

02:58:01.270 --> 02:58:01.570
Wellby: And-

02:58:01.990 --> 02:58:02.110
Unknown: Yeah

02:58:02.110 --> 02:58:09.350
Wellby: ... if she is Fae, she also met us after immediately hearing a story of how we freed someone trapped by a Fae and then killed them.

02:58:13.090 --> 02:58:13.390
Seeker: Wait, who-

02:58:14.450 --> 02:58:15.850
DM: So in the morning-

02:58:15.850 --> 02:58:17.470
Seeker: [laughs] Nice. Thanks, dude

02:58:18.790 --> 02:58:19.270
DM: ... uh,

02:58:20.130 --> 02:58:25.170
DM: do you wanna talk to the, go try and find the priest before you meet Nika, or do you wanna just-

02:58:25.390 --> 02:58:27.210
Unknown: I wanna talk to the elf one

02:58:27.210 --> 02:58:27.510
DM: Okay.

02:58:28.770 --> 02:58:30.730
Seeker: Well, I guess Delwath's in charge.

02:58:30.730 --> 02:58:31.390
Wellby: [laughs]

02:58:31.410 --> 02:58:32.370
DM: Let's go and talk to the elf.

02:58:32.370 --> 02:58:34.430
Unknown: You're a good split up. [laughs]

02:58:34.430 --> 02:58:35.930
Seeker: Now we're all going to talk to the elf.

02:58:35.930 --> 02:58:39.150
Delwath: But I think also try and find the Skaer.

02:58:39.150 --> 02:58:42.330
Delwath: I actually wanna know more about the Skaer before we approach the priest.

02:58:43.090 --> 02:58:45.730
Delwath: The priest seems like more likely to not wanna talk to us

02:58:46.990 --> 02:58:49.070
Delwath: than a trade emissary.

02:58:49.350 --> 02:58:50.430
Delwath: It would be good to just, like,

02:58:52.670 --> 02:58:56.650
Delwath: find out... Like I feel like none of us know anything at all about the Skaer.

02:58:57.630 --> 02:58:59.810
Unknown: Well, we're gonna a little bit.

02:58:59.830 --> 02:58:59.970
Delwath: Hmm?

02:59:00.810 --> 02:59:01.410
Delwath: Wellby might know.

