DM: Yeah, I mean, so Wellby's impression is they're, they're a pretty insular society.

02:59:06.110 --> 02:59:12.110
DM: Like you see, you see people, you see like young Skaer, like often will like just wander around.

02:59:12.110 --> 02:59:16.130
DM: Like you can even work with some, like there was a, you know, like a, you know, a

02:59:17.390 --> 02:59:20.450
DM: 19-year-old or something who's spending a year working on your ship.

02:59:21.830 --> 02:59:24.450
DM: They're one of the few humans that will...

02:59:24.450 --> 02:59:26.810
DM: Or, or a ship you knew. It might not have been your ship.

02:59:27.870 --> 02:59:32.210
DM: But they, when, you know, they rarely settle down anywhere other than

02:59:34.270 --> 02:59:37.630
DM: in their like small island home.

02:59:37.630 --> 02:59:39.430
DM: So there's not a lot of Skaer... There's not like a

02:59:40.210 --> 02:59:41.450
DM: s- a particularly big...

02:59:41.450 --> 02:59:47.670
DM: I mean, there are a few Skaer ex- expats, like living in Poland and elsewhere, but like mostly it seems like they,

02:59:48.770 --> 02:59:50.430
DM: like you'll see 'em wandering around.

02:59:50.430 --> 02:59:56.390
DM: They have a reputation to the south in Sembara as like raiders basically.

02:59:56.390 --> 03:00:02.310
DM: But from your experience, they're not, like they rarely leave their islands and they're not, they don't seem like they're-

03:00:02.350 --> 03:00:03.550
Delwath: Are they humans?

03:00:03.550 --> 03:00:04.230
DM: Yeah, they're humans.

03:00:07.290 --> 03:00:10.730
DM: And they're unusual 'cause they worship a totally different god from anybody else.

03:00:10.730 --> 03:00:13.170
Unknown: They worship Kaikkea, the ocean mother.

03:00:16.930 --> 03:00:18.070
Seeker: Who Wellby saw one time.

03:00:18.850 --> 03:00:19.230
Seeker: Um-

03:00:19.370 --> 03:00:19.930
Delwath: Wellby what?

03:00:20.310 --> 03:00:21.090
Seeker: Saw one time.

03:00:21.390 --> 03:00:21.970
Delwath: Maybe.

03:00:21.970 --> 03:00:22.950
Seeker: He did?

03:00:22.970 --> 03:00:23.430
Delwath: Well...

03:00:24.450 --> 03:00:25.930
Wellby: The dragon with the ocean mother guy?

03:00:26.270 --> 03:00:26.670
Seeker: Absolutely.

03:00:26.670 --> 03:00:27.710
Wellby: That's amazing. I love it.

03:00:27.710 --> 03:00:28.070
Kenzo: Same, kind of.

03:00:28.770 --> 03:00:34.130
Wellby: Oh, that was in the Green Sea, or no, no, no, that was in the bay and they're in the Green Sea, the Skaer Islands?

03:00:34.190 --> 03:00:35.010
DM: Yeah, they're like-

03:00:35.090 --> 03:00:35.210
Wellby: Oh

03:00:35.210 --> 03:00:36.530
DM: ... outside. They're like in the...

03:00:36.530 --> 03:00:43.190
DM: I mean, they're, they're, you know, at one point their territory stretched into the Western Gulf pre-Drancore, but they sort of

03:00:44.850 --> 03:00:46.690
DM: never really reclaimed the-

03:00:46.710 --> 03:00:46.930
Delwath: Mm

03:00:46.930 --> 03:00:48.310
DM: ... extent of that

03:00:49.770 --> 03:00:53.750
DM: empire. And, and now they're, they don't trade much, right?

03:00:53.750 --> 03:00:57.110
DM: Like they, I mean, their, their, this volcanic

03:00:58.250 --> 03:01:05.030
DM: steel, the Skaer steel is like really valuable, but they don't s- they don't like trade it a ton.

03:01:05.030 --> 03:01:05.710
DM: They're not like-

03:01:06.090 --> 03:01:06.210
Delwath: Mm.

03:01:07.610 --> 03:01:10.950
DM: They don't really, they don't have like merchant fleets, right?

03:01:10.970 --> 03:01:14.670
DM: Like halflings don't usually stop in the islands because

03:01:15.730 --> 03:01:17.550
DM: they don't have like mercer towns.

03:01:17.550 --> 03:01:18.270
DM: There's no like-

03:01:18.950 --> 03:01:19.669
Delwath: Mm.

03:01:19.669 --> 03:01:30.210
DM: You know, sometimes you'll sail past and like, you know, you'll stop and, you know, they'll want something and you'll sell it to them and get, you know, a little bit of something in return.

03:01:30.210 --> 03:01:30.390
DM: But,

03:01:31.490 --> 03:01:32.910
DM: so they do seem kind of

03:01:34.310 --> 03:01:34.890
DM: insular.

03:01:38.350 --> 03:01:41.190
DM: But also in your experience, not unfriendly, right?

03:01:41.190 --> 03:01:43.690
DM: Like, especially the like, the like,

03:01:44.570 --> 03:01:45.350
DM: you know, the sort of,

03:01:47.190 --> 03:01:54.870
DM: you know, 19 to 22-year-old diaspora that seems to be quite common, like spread out around the-

03:01:56.890 --> 03:01:57.090
Wellby: Where?

03:01:57.470 --> 03:01:57.850
DM: Um-

03:01:57.850 --> 03:01:58.870
Wellby: Checking eye color.

03:02:01.230 --> 03:02:01.730
Wellby: No? No.

03:02:01.750 --> 03:02:02.430
Wellby: Around the...

03:02:05.550 --> 03:02:05.730
DM: Um,

03:02:07.750 --> 03:02:09.430
DM: yeah, that's pretty much what you know about them.

03:02:09.430 --> 03:02:11.470
DM: They're incredibly good navigators.

03:02:11.470 --> 03:02:15.170
DM: Like the currents in the Skaer Islands are nasty.

03:02:15.710 --> 03:02:17.690
DM: Like even halfling ships don't...

03:02:17.690 --> 03:02:27.690
DM: try to avoid navigating through the islands 'cause there'll be like sudden giant waves that just, you know, appear out of nowhere or like whirlpools or like

03:02:28.870 --> 03:02:33.170
DM: steam and mist from where lava hits the ocean that obscures-

03:02:33.290 --> 03:02:34.210
Wellby: Mm

03:02:34.210 --> 03:02:36.070
DM: ... um, sailing for miles.

03:02:36.070 --> 03:02:38.710
DM: They're not easy places to sail.

03:02:39.550 --> 03:02:41.170
Unknown: Tricky currents, tricky winds.

03:02:50.890 --> 03:02:51.190
DM: So...

03:02:53.350 --> 03:02:55.310
DM: Maybe do a little bit in the morning and then-

03:02:55.390 --> 03:02:55.550
DM: Yeah

03:02:55.550 --> 03:03:00.250
DM: ... stop before any super major encounters.

03:03:00.310 --> 03:03:00.570
DM: Yeah.

03:03:01.810 --> 03:03:03.390
DM: But the question is where are you going?

03:03:03.390 --> 03:03:03.690
Seeker: That.

03:03:04.830 --> 03:03:05.430
DM: Are you going?

03:03:05.490 --> 03:03:06.270
Seeker: Yeah, I think so.

03:03:07.250 --> 03:03:07.430
Unknown: Sure

03:03:12.220 --> 03:03:12.440
DM: Okay.

03:03:13.600 --> 03:03:15.200
DM: He's easy enough to find.

03:03:16.180 --> 03:03:16.580
DM: Um...

03:03:17.640 --> 03:03:18.320
Kenzo: Nice.

03:03:20.059 --> 03:03:21.080
Kenzo: These are so good too.

03:03:23.980 --> 03:03:25.960
DM: This is what I did instead of writing my talk.

03:03:25.960 --> 03:03:27.660
DM: [laughs]

03:03:27.680 --> 03:03:28.560
Kenzo: We'll write your talk for you.

03:03:28.680 --> 03:03:29.980
DM: I, I have some time.

03:03:31.260 --> 03:03:32.740
DM: I can work on it Saturday morning.

03:03:34.000 --> 03:03:34.260
DM: Um,

03:03:37.120 --> 03:03:46.020
DM: so, um, I, I mean, it's easy to, to find, and you presumably send a message ahead, and he's happy to, you know, meet with another elf any time.

03:03:46.020 --> 03:03:46.200
DM: Um,

03:03:48.480 --> 03:03:50.640
Unknown: here, let's change the tavern music.

03:03:54.060 --> 03:03:54.320
DM: Um,

03:03:55.460 --> 03:03:57.540
Unknown: let me just go in my journal to my music.

03:03:58.000 --> 03:03:58.120
DM: Uh...

03:03:58.120 --> 03:04:09.800
Kenzo: [upbeat medieval music]

03:04:09.820 --> 03:04:11.220
Kenzo: Oh, nice. What's the name of the elf?

03:04:12.180 --> 03:04:12.440
Kenzo: Mel-

03:04:13.040 --> 03:04:13.900
DM: Melindir.

03:04:13.900 --> 03:04:14.480
Kenzo: Melindir.

03:04:16.259 --> 03:04:17.540
Kenzo: Uh, is that elf-y like Elfstein?

03:04:17.920 --> 03:04:21.740
DM: So you, so you send a message ahead, and, and you approach.

03:04:21.760 --> 03:04:23.000
DM: And the, um...

03:04:23.000 --> 03:04:30.200
DM: So he lives, again, in this sort of relatively fancy neighborhood, like west of the bridge.

03:04:30.200 --> 03:04:30.440
DM: Um,

03:04:33.180 --> 03:04:40.420
DM: you know, it's, you know, you walk, you walk along, and you can see that the buildings are getting a little bit more, um,

03:04:43.120 --> 03:04:46.160
DM: you know, richer and, um...

03:04:46.160 --> 03:04:53.260
DM: There's like, you know, uh, banks here and, and sort of a lot of the guilds have headquarters here.

03:04:53.260 --> 03:05:03.300
DM: This is... There's this big cathedral that's under construction, a temple to the War Lord, one of the, um, eight divines, sponsored by the Shipwrights Guild.

03:05:04.120 --> 03:05:04.360
DM: Um,

03:05:05.620 --> 03:05:09.460
DM: there's merchant, there's like merchant palaces in this area, too.

03:05:09.880 --> 03:05:13.640
Kenzo: You know, Delwath, I was, I was always curious, are there poor elves?

03:05:14.620 --> 03:05:15.940
Kenzo: Are there elves that are like,

03:05:17.280 --> 03:05:21.600
Kenzo: you know, have bad attitudes and poor manners that are just like more...

03:05:23.100 --> 03:05:25.720
Unknown: You know? Are there like lower class elves?

03:05:29.520 --> 03:05:30.120
Delwath: There are

03:05:32.600 --> 03:05:34.280
Delwath: many different personalities.

03:05:35.260 --> 03:05:36.500
Delwath: There are certainly elves who

03:05:38.420 --> 03:05:41.380
Unknown: are unpleasant or mean or-

03:05:41.380 --> 03:05:43.160
Kenzo: We know

03:05:43.160 --> 03:05:44.700
Delwath: ... even perhaps condescending.

03:05:44.700 --> 03:05:46.780
Kenzo: [laughs]

03:05:46.780 --> 03:05:46.960
DM: [laughs]

03:05:46.980 --> 03:05:47.760
Kenzo: And patronizing.

03:05:47.760 --> 03:05:48.860
DM: [laughs]

03:05:49.080 --> 03:05:49.200
Delwath: Um,

03:05:50.900 --> 03:05:51.080
Delwath: but

03:05:53.580 --> 03:05:55.240
Delwath: there's no poverty.

03:05:56.380 --> 03:05:57.420
Delwath: There's no...

03:05:59.320 --> 03:06:00.340
Delwath: You know, as Wellby said,

03:06:01.220 --> 03:06:05.080
Unknown: amongst the halflings, with the elves too, no one's left behind.

03:06:05.800 --> 03:06:08.600
Delwath: It's not familial like the halflings are.

03:06:08.600 --> 03:06:11.500
Delwath: It's...

03:06:11.500 --> 03:06:15.780
Delwath: We don't grow up close to our birth parents.

03:06:15.780 --> 03:06:16.580
DM: That's right.

03:06:16.680 --> 03:06:21.920
Kenzo: Oh, that's right. I remember, uh, that giant tree where there's like the little baby elves who are just-

03:06:21.920 --> 03:06:22.100
Delwath: Yeah

03:06:22.100 --> 03:06:23.400
DM: ... like crop and harvest.

03:06:23.480 --> 03:06:27.280
Unknown: Yeah. Every generation is born around the same time,

03:06:29.900 --> 03:06:31.860
Unknown: and so we grow up closer to our

03:06:33.740 --> 03:06:35.580
Unknown: year mates, our siblings,

03:06:36.780 --> 03:06:39.160
Delwath: than the other generations.

03:06:39.180 --> 03:06:40.140
Delwath: But...

03:06:40.140 --> 03:06:41.540
Kenzo: There... Are, are there any outcasts?

03:06:43.540 --> 03:06:45.580
Kenzo: Those that don't fit, those that don't belong?

03:06:47.600 --> 03:06:49.400
Unknown: It's not that simple. There,

03:06:50.520 --> 03:06:53.860
Unknown: there are elves who are cast out, but it's quite

03:06:55.640 --> 03:06:56.880
Delwath: rare.

03:06:56.880 --> 03:06:57.680
Delwath: I think-

03:06:57.680 --> 03:06:58.600
Kenzo: I'd like to meet one.

03:07:00.260 --> 03:07:01.360
Delwath: It's not normally

03:07:04.640 --> 03:07:07.880
Delwath: an elf you would want to meet, I think.

03:07:07.880 --> 03:07:08.580
Delwath: It is not...

03:07:10.760 --> 03:07:12.900
Unknown: Elven society is very accommodating to

03:07:14.740 --> 03:07:15.700
Delwath: personalities.

03:07:16.680 --> 03:07:17.080
Kenzo: Hm.

03:07:17.080 --> 03:07:19.160
Delwath: Outcasts are more-

03:07:19.220 --> 03:07:20.760
Unknown: They've, they've violated something.

03:07:21.340 --> 03:07:21.940
Delwath: Yeah.

03:07:21.960 --> 03:07:22.380
Kenzo: Hm.

03:07:22.380 --> 03:07:23.780
Delwath: They're m- they're more,

03:07:25.080 --> 03:07:25.380
Delwath: um...

03:07:29.480 --> 03:07:35.500
Unknown: They've, they've broken the, the bond in some fashion that sort of holds the generations together.

03:07:35.520 --> 03:07:35.880
Kenzo: Hm.

03:07:36.000 --> 03:07:37.020
DM: I see. Interesting.

03:07:37.040 --> 03:07:38.760
Delwath: And we have...

03:07:39.760 --> 03:07:40.980
Delwath: You have to remember, we don't...

03:07:43.880 --> 03:07:48.980
Delwath: The oldest elf I've heard of has been alive since the beginning of the world.

03:07:48.980 --> 03:07:51.800
DM: [laughs]

03:07:51.860 --> 03:07:52.680
Kenzo: That's pretty old.

03:07:55.680 --> 03:07:55.780
Delwath: It,

03:07:56.940 --> 03:07:56.960
Delwath: it-

03:07:57.120 --> 03:07:57.560
Kenzo: Oh,

03:07:58.440 --> 03:07:59.600
Kenzo: that's amazing

03:07:59.600 --> 03:08:01.880
Unknown: ... it, it may sound condescending, but it's-

03:08:02.780 --> 03:08:04.380
Unknown: No, it's, I'm genuinely amazed.

03:08:04.620 --> 03:08:04.840
Delwath: It is-

03:08:04.840 --> 03:08:05.820
Kenzo: I'm genuinely amazed

03:08:05.820 --> 03:08:07.420
Unknown: ... I, I have not met them.

03:08:08.520 --> 03:08:08.820
Delwath: Um,

03:08:10.020 --> 03:08:11.480
Delwath: but, but, uh,

03:08:12.460 --> 03:08:13.120
Delwath: some of my,

03:08:13.940 --> 03:08:16.020
Delwath: uh, generation, generation mates did.

03:08:16.620 --> 03:08:17.100
Kenzo: Wow.

03:08:17.100 --> 03:08:17.360
Delwath: Um,

03:08:18.860 --> 03:08:21.900
Delwath: it is, it gets harder as we age to

03:08:22.920 --> 03:08:24.380
Delwath: remember to stay alive.

03:08:25.880 --> 03:08:27.680
Delwath: But no elf has ever died

03:08:29.200 --> 03:08:30.480
Delwath: of old age unwillingly.

03:08:33.480 --> 03:08:33.560
Kenzo: Hm.

03:08:33.560 --> 03:08:34.380
Delwath: So it, it...

03:08:37.180 --> 03:08:38.280
Delwath: But there's so few of us.

03:08:39.400 --> 03:08:39.560
Delwath: It,

03:08:40.740 --> 03:08:42.380
Delwath: we feel very...

03:08:42.380 --> 03:08:45.020
Unknown: And of course, magic flows through our societies, right?

03:08:45.920 --> 03:08:48.800
Delwath: Material plenty is less of an issue than many others.

03:08:49.500 --> 03:08:49.660
Kenzo: Hm.

03:08:51.100 --> 03:08:52.460
Kenzo: I apologize for the diversion.

03:08:52.460 --> 03:08:57.420
Kenzo: I just feel like whenever we go to see an elf, it's always in the finest part of town, so I was just curious about that.

03:08:57.420 --> 03:08:59.440
Unknown: Delwath, I'm, I'm forgetting.

03:08:59.440 --> 03:09:00.280
DM: What other elves

03:09:01.300 --> 03:09:04.000
Wellby: have we run into over this last year in Morre?

03:09:05.180 --> 03:09:06.780
Unknown: There was, um, what was his name?

03:09:06.780 --> 03:09:07.560
Delwath: Melangar?

03:09:08.320 --> 03:09:09.160
Delwath: Melangar.

03:09:09.580 --> 03:09:09.820
DM: Melangar.

03:09:09.820 --> 03:09:10.200
Delwath: He was-

03:09:10.300 --> 03:09:12.560
Kenzo: There was a big elf that's dragon.

03:09:12.560 --> 03:09:13.120
Delwath: Melangar-

03:09:13.540 --> 03:09:14.180
DM: Yeah.

03:09:14.200 --> 03:09:15.400
Delwath: Melangar was, um-

03:09:15.400 --> 03:09:16.640
Kenzo: [laughs]

03:09:18.032 --> 03:09:20.092
Wellby: Give me confidence. [laughs]

03:09:20.092 --> 03:09:20.892
Delwath: [laughs] Um

03:09:20.892 --> 03:09:23.732
Unknown: But also the fancy room in your head.

03:09:23.732 --> 03:09:25.672
Unknown: I, we have not met many, and-

03:09:26.032 --> 03:09:27.012
Wellby: Wait, wait, sorry. Who was Bel-

03:09:27.052 --> 03:09:28.072
Delwath: Belangor was...

03:09:28.932 --> 03:09:31.372
Unknown: He was, um, he lived in the Dunmar Fellowship

03:09:31.372 --> 03:09:34.032
DM: He had come and tried to talk to the fake elf.

03:09:34.111 --> 03:09:34.232
Delwath: Yeah

03:09:34.232 --> 03:09:35.772
Unknown: ... and like run away from him.

03:09:36.072 --> 03:09:37.372
Delwath: Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah. He was like the psychic-

03:09:37.432 --> 03:09:38.752
DM: And hid out in the-

03:09:39.272 --> 03:09:39.612
Delwath: Right

03:09:39.612 --> 03:09:40.992
DM: ... pocket dimension with

03:09:42.332 --> 03:09:44.292
DM: all of those Denikari who had the

03:09:44.752 --> 03:09:45.552
Delwath: But he was, um,

03:09:47.732 --> 03:09:48.372
Delwath: he was

03:09:50.432 --> 03:09:52.872
Delwath: Delwath's generation. You, I vaguely knew him.

03:09:52.912 --> 03:09:53.052
Unknown: Yeah.

03:09:53.052 --> 03:09:54.292
Delwath: He was like a friend of a...

03:09:54.292 --> 03:09:55.452
Delwath: He was like not from my

03:09:56.692 --> 03:09:58.992
Delwath: home area, but nearby.

03:09:58.992 --> 03:10:07.552
Wellby: Does that mean then, Delwath, that this person is like the first elf in the world you've met since coming back again?

03:10:07.792 --> 03:10:08.352
Delwath: Yes.

03:10:10.512 --> 03:10:12.912
Wellby: What? How is that going to be?

03:10:12.912 --> 03:10:19.252
Delwath: [sighs] I've been avoiding it for some time.

03:10:20.552 --> 03:10:20.912
Wellby: Huh?

03:10:23.072 --> 03:10:23.252
Delwath: [sighs]

03:10:23.271 --> 03:10:24.492
Wellby: You know what they say about your fears.

03:10:25.332 --> 03:10:25.672
Delwath: Well,

03:10:27.692 --> 03:10:28.112
Delwath: so...

03:10:28.112 --> 03:10:30.872
Wellby: [laughs]

03:10:30.912 --> 03:10:32.832
Delwath: Yes, I do know what they say about your fears.

03:10:33.792 --> 03:10:38.352
Delwath: You have to understand, the, the way elven society is structured, there are...

03:10:40.852 --> 03:10:44.472
Delwath: It's hard being gone from the world for so long.

03:10:44.472 --> 03:10:45.712
Delwath: You, you miss things.

03:10:47.512 --> 03:10:49.092
Delwath: You miss opportunities.

03:10:53.972 --> 03:10:54.592
Delwath: It's been,

03:10:56.352 --> 03:10:56.712
Delwath: been

03:10:57.712 --> 03:11:04.892
Delwath: hiding away from even thinking about my people 'cause I feel like they're lost to me in some way.

03:11:06.072 --> 03:11:06.312
Unknown: Huh.

03:11:07.892 --> 03:11:10.812
Unknown: Are you an outcast?

03:11:10.932 --> 03:11:14.652
Kenzo: I was just gonna say, I feel like I've just been in my whole life with an outcast.

03:11:14.652 --> 03:11:15.592
Unknown: [laughs]

03:11:16.712 --> 03:11:21.492
Unknown: Of elven society. Um, I, I was a, I was a quartermaster in, in my,

03:11:22.832 --> 03:11:26.511
Unknown: in a company of soldiers in, during the Great War.

03:11:27.112 --> 03:11:32.352
Wellby: You were indeed, but the tense of that verb is not the present.

03:11:35.712 --> 03:11:36.912
Delwath: Since

03:11:38.592 --> 03:11:45.512
Delwath: I have not rejoined or made any attempt to rejoin elven society since returning, 'cause

03:11:46.672 --> 03:11:47.712
Delwath: it's too sad.

03:11:49.092 --> 03:11:51.292
Delwath: I, I've missed my generation.

03:11:51.312 --> 03:11:53.052
Unknown: I, I will never have children.

03:11:53.052 --> 03:11:56.172
Delwath: I will never continue the cycle of

03:11:57.432 --> 03:11:57.912
Delwath: elven

03:11:59.512 --> 03:12:03.072
Unknown: life. It's, it, it's moved on.

03:12:03.092 --> 03:12:04.132
Delwath: It's too late for me.

03:12:04.972 --> 03:12:08.292
Wellby: That is much more tragic than I realized.

03:12:08.292 --> 03:12:08.592
Delwath: Yes.

03:12:09.772 --> 03:12:10.772
Wellby: Wow.

03:12:10.772 --> 03:12:10.912
Delwath: It,

03:12:12.472 --> 03:12:12.872
Delwath: we don't,

03:12:14.572 --> 03:12:20.192
Delwath: we don't... Elves live for many years, but there's only a small window where we form families,

03:12:21.092 --> 03:12:31.132
Delwath: and then they dissipate again, and, and our long life is more complex than a simple family

03:12:31.132 --> 03:12:31.892
Delwath: relationship.

03:12:32.552 --> 03:12:32.612
Wellby: Yeah.

03:12:32.612 --> 03:12:35.412
Delwath: And for my generation, that time has come and gone.

03:12:38.172 --> 03:12:43.672
